 target; `nbody` (1.32×) and `double_reduction` (1.18×) are the same FP-kernel
 family and are likely to share a root cause with it.
+
+## Audit (2026-09-05, session 8) — red-team of #412–#418; rebase; width-test fix
+
+### Upstream defect fixed: width unit test contradicted the width table
+
+`declared_width_agrees_with_the_lane_count_in_the_name` asserted
+`VecSubI32x8 / VecAndI32x8 / VecOrI32x8 / VecXorI32x8 == Some(16)` — the four
+ops were pasted into the 128-bit `narrow` list by the same commit that added
+them, while `vector_result_width` correctly reports `Some(32)` (8 lanes × 4 B;
+codegen lowers via `emit_avx_binary_256` on `%ymm`). Implementation right,
+test data wrong. The test was rewritten to be **exhaustive by construction**:
+it extracts every `Vec*` variant from the enum via `include_str!` at compile
+time and derives the expected width from the name's last `<Type>x<Lanes>`
+token (documented divergences: `Horizontal*` → None, `VecStore*` → None
+except the deliberate `VecStoreI64x2`, unlowered `Sadalp/Smlal` → None). A
+future op added to the enum is checked automatically; the hand-list failure
+mode that produced this bug cannot recur. Mechanical verification over the
+full enum found no other table/name disagreement.
+
+### Guard placement: upstream right, our hoist a latent miscompile
+
+Our local branch hoisted the non-IV-phi carried-value guard from
+`analyze_map_pattern`/`analyze_stencil_pattern` into `analyze_loop_pattern`.
+Rebase repro showed `vectorize_carried_value_and_negzero` failing
+(`k_acc(1) = 0 want 3`): `analyze_loop_pattern` is the **matmul** analyzer,
+not a shared entry — its `None` falls through the dispatcher's else-if chain
+to analyzers that (in our revision) no longer had the guard. Upstream's
+per-analyzer placement is correct; kept. The hoist is recorded here so it is
+not re-proposed.
+
+### Ported from the local branch (A/B-measured on current upstream)
+
+1. `memfold_consumer_256`: fold gates for the four integer lane ops.
+   Without: xor kernel emits `vmovdqu` loads + stack round-trips; with:
+   `vpxor (mem), %ymm, %ymm`. `is_vec_ssa_producer` gains the same four
+   families for list consistency; on today's upstream the omission is
+   correctness-neutral (deferred-store path reorganized in #413/#416 — the
+   historical segfault claim does not reproduce at -O2/-O3, v3/SSE2, stack
+   or static storage, or under CCC_NO_SMALL_SLOTS), so the entries are
+   hardening, not a live fix.
+2. i686 whole-function GPR liveness oracle for `fold_memory_operands`
+   (barrier-assumed deadness was unsound for register-allocated values:
+   `maxi(a,b){return a>b?a:b;}` param home folded across the select's
+   conditional jump). Spot-verified: maxi keeps param homes; divmod's
+   `cltd`/`idivl` implicit `edx:eax` handling survives renaming.
+3. Tests: `vex_promote_semantic.c` and the richer
+   `vectorize_int_map_lanes.c` (0..17 sweep, I64x2, both broadcast orders,
+   all four strict min/max folds + two non-strict no-folds, NaN/±0 pairings,
+   in-place aliasing).
+
+### Adopted as-is (audited, no defects found)
+
+#412 five miscompiles + RA cost model; #413 if-convert deref coverage, C23
+`va_start`, `folded_read_points`, vex BFS, xmm2 confinement; #414 lane ops +
+carried-value guard + `-0.0` data emission + clamp fold; #415 cast-peel
+injectivity + RA-06 (off by default, documented); #416 wider slot roots;
+#417 docs; #418 epilogue cross-jumping (soundness gates audited: runs
+rejected on labels, whole-run replacement, per-function CFI bail, return
+regs untouched; known trade-off — exact-text merging can grow byte size for
+2–3-insn epilogues since `jmp rel32` is 5 bytes; insn count is the canonical
+metric here; LCS extension is CG-09).
+
+Verification: `cargo test --lib` 1956/1956; regression suite 626 PASS /
+0 FAIL / 15 SKIP (ELF32 — no runner on this host); map_sub emits `vpsubd`,
+4×4 matmul 16× `vfmadd`, i64 reduction `paddq`.
